# The llama.cpp source openvibes-llm builds llama-server from (assistant
# spec §6, §10). Read by scripts/build-llama-server.sh.
#
# The source is the upstream release ggml-org/llama.cpp v0.9.0 (tag object
# c4261a74a59c, commit below). The release publishes no source tarball asset,
# so this is GitHub's archive of the tag. GitHub generates archives on demand;
# their bytes have been stable but are not guaranteed. If the SHA-256 check
# ever fails, re-verify before re-pinning: download the archive into an empty
# directory, check `gzip -dc <tarball> | git get-tar-commit-id` prints
# LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT, and check the tag still resolves to it
# (`gh api /repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/tags/<tag object> --jq .object.sha`).
#
# To update: pick a newer release tag, resolve its commit as above, check the
# upstream security advisories (github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/security and the
# GitHub Advisory Database) for fixes and open issues, in particular
# GHSA-6hc7-9rph-cm99 / CVE-2026-43631 (use-after-free when the server sleeps;
# keep --sleep-idle-seconds off until an advisory names a fixed release),
# update all three values, rebuild, check every CMake option the build script
# passes still exists, and run `openvibes-admin assistant eval`.
LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT=cd959bae99ff4bed22bef2604f45241c09bbb8c8
LLAMA_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.0.tar.gz
LLAMA_SOURCE_SHA256=5d0f1aaf55fd8629c29a55e81b7cb63b80239f83c33a580963071204896836a8
